  "note": "Election of the Cookstown Urban District Council, ordinary day 17 May 1961; only the twelve Unionist candidates were nominated, so there was no contest (Mid-Ulster Mail, 6 May 1961, p. 1). 'As expected only the twelve Unionist candidates were nominated on Wednesday for the twelve seats on Cookstown Urban Council. Consequently there will be no contest.' Miss Dunphy and Dr. Elliott were new members; Messrs. Gough and Newell did not seek re-election. Returned unopposed."
